		{"id":"d2","type":"text","text":"`donations_db`","x":1110,"y":580,"width":220,"height":90,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"d3","type":"text","text":"`catalog_db`","x":1340,"y":580,"width":220,"height":90,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"d4","type":"text","text":"`receipts_db`","x":1570,"y":580,"width":220,"height":90,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"d5","type":"text","text":"`fundraising_db`","x":1800,"y":580,"width":220,"height":90,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"rules","type":"text","text":"# The two irreversible precautions\n🔴 **No cross-temple SQL**\n🔴 **No cross-temple foreign keys**\nTwo shards make both physically impossible.\n\n# k3s operating rules\n1. **All manifests in git** — Flux makes this a mechanism, not a habit\n2. **Upgrade k3s once a year** — the same restart renews its internal TLS certificates\n3. **AWS permissions:** narrow shared node role now → **OIDC-based per-service roles (IRSA-style) before the first temple goes live.** Never long-lived access keys\n4. ECR pulls need a containerd credential helper or a token-refresh CronJob\n5. **Rehearse the node rebuild in UAT** — single-node prod makes rebuild time the real availability number\n6. **Back up the `age` key** to the password manager\n\n# Supporting precautions\n🟠 Registry resolves temple → host; no hard-coded DB URLs\n🟠 Datasources lazy, cached, refreshable without restart\n🟠 Migration fan-out driven by the registry, grouped by shard\n🟠 Temple context on every service hop and every async job\n🟡 Database names constant across shards; only host varies\n🟡 Uniform schema naming `t_<temple>`\n🟡 `SET LOCAL`, never session `SET`\n🟡 Per-schema dump/restore tooling, tested\n🟡 Pool sizes configured per shard\n🟡 Registry cache TTL + invalidation","x":2200,"y":-270,"width":440,"height":800,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"a-out","type":"text","text":"**Transactional Outbox**\nevent written atomically with the DB change\n_this is also your replay log_","x":160,"y":275,"width":340,"height":100},
		{"id":"a-broker","type":"text","text":"## RabbitMQ\n**in-cluster StatefulSet**\ndurable queues · persistent messages · EBS volume","x":540,"y":275,"width":340,"height":100,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"a-idem","type":"text","text":"**Idempotent consumers**\n+ idempotency keys on money calls","x":1300,"y":275,"width":340,"height":100},
		{"id":"a-dlq","type":"text","text":"**Retries · DLQ · replay**\na vendor outage never loses a receipt","x":1680,"y":275,"width":370,"height":100},
		{"id":"pgb","type":"text","text":"## PgBouncer\n**transaction pooling** from day one\n\nForces `SET LOCAL search_path`\ninside the transaction —\nnever a session-level `SET`","x":160,"y":510,"width":280,"height":200,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"sh-noida","type":"text","text":"### shard-noida — **SILO**\nNoida alone","x":480,"y":510,"width":300,"height":150,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"notin","type":"text","text":"## Deliberately NOT in this architecture\n_so none of it gets re-proposed_\n\n❌ Data warehouse / cross-temple queries\n❌ Kafka — RabbitMQ chosen; the outbox is the replay log\n❌ Amazon MQ — the outbox already de-risks what it would buy\n❌ EKS · ECS · Docker Compose in production\n❌ ArgoCD — ~1 GB for a UI; Flux gives the mechanism\n❌ A two-node cluster — that is not HA; real HA is three servers\n❌ Database-per-temple (Model A) — 8,000 connections\n❌ Shared schema + `tenant_id` (Model C) — one missing `WHERE` leaks donor PII\n❌ Long-lived AWS access keys\n❌ Server-side rendering / Next.js — no Open Graph tags or SEO in use today\n❌ AWS DMS — CDC buys nothing for a big-bang cutover of 2.95 GB\n❌ A separate Time Management app, API, domain or deploy","x":2200,"y":570,"width":440,"height":440,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"s-users","type":"text","text":"### Users & People\n`users_db`","x":160,"y":-310,"width":290,"height":100,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"s-rec","type":"text","text":"### Receipts & 80G\n`receipts_db`\n_rendering only_","x":1120,"y":-310,"width":290,"height":100,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"s-fr","type":"text","text":"### Fundraising\n`fundraising_db`","x":1440,"y":-310,"width":290,"height":100,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"s-ev","type":"text","text":"### Events & Volunteering\n`events_db`","x":1760,"y":-310,"width":290,"height":100,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"s-ops","type":"text","text":"### Ops long tail\n`ops_db` — POS · cash · HR · attendance · gifts · TR books","x":160,"y":-180,"width":290,"height":100,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"auditlib","type":"text","text":"### Audit = a shared Java LIBRARY, not a service\nEvery service writes its audit rows into **its own database, in the temple's own schema** — next to the data they describe. No extra database per temple · no service writes into another's data · invisible across temples by construction.","x":800,"y":-180,"width":1250,"height":100,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"p-not","type":"text","text":"### Notifications\n`notifications_db`\nWhatsApp · SMS · Email · **FCM push**","x":160,"y":55,"width":300,"height":100,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"p-file","type":"text","text":"### Files & Documents\n`files_db` + S3","x":490,"y":55,"width":300,"height":100,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"auth","type":"text","text":"### Auth service\nlogin · token issue\nsession management\n\n_an outage here ≠ a platform outage_","x":530,"y":-650,"width":290,"height":170,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"rbac","type":"text","text":"### Authorization\nThe token carries: **who you are · which temples you belong to · a coarse role in each**.\nServices resolve fine-grained permissions, **cached once per request** — this is the fix for today's N+1.\n\n🔴 Today's `users.role_id` is a **single global role** and cannot carry over. **Role-per-temple is required**, whatever else changes.","x":850,"y":-650,"width":350,"height":170,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"registry","type":"text","text":"## Tenant Registry\n**control plane**\ntemple → **shard host** · domain · status · plan · onboarding state\n_zero hard-coded DB URLs anywhere_","x":1230,"y":-650,"width":360,"height":170,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"config","type":"text","text":"**Config & flags**\nper-temple\nrollout rings","x":1620,"y":-650,"width":200,"height":170},
		{"id":"cpdb","type":"text","text":"**Control-plane DB**\nsingle\nnot sharded","x":1850,"y":-650,"width":190,"height":170,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"s-don","type":"text","text":"### Donations + Payments\n`donations_db`\n_receipt numbering lives here_","x":480,"y":-310,"width":290,"height":100,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"s-cat","type":"text","text":"### Catalog & Settings\n`catalog_db`","x":800,"y":-310,"width":290,"height":100,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"s-tm","type":"text","text":"### Time Management\n`timemgmt_db`\n_out of scope for now_","x":480,"y":-180,"width":290,"height":100,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"notes","type":"text","text":"# Decisions locked\n\n**Backend** Java 25 LTS · Maven · Spring Boot microservices · Spring Data JPA (CRUD) + jOOQ (reporting) · JobRunr · Flyway\n\n**Orchestration** **k3s, self-hosted**, single node on **t4g (Graviton)**. $0 control plane. Kubernetes from day one, so there is no future migration; EKS later = pointing `kubectl` elsewhere.\n\n**Deployment** **Flux (GitOps)**. The cluster pulls from git and self-heals drift. Jenkins builds and pushes images, updates the manifest tag, and never holds cluster credentials.\n\n**Secrets** SOPS + age, encrypted in git, decrypted by Flux.\n\n**Data** **Model D (bridge)**, built D-minimal. Two shards in every environment from day one. Prod day-1: `shard-noida` (silo) + `shard-pool-1` (GNW, NEX, WHF).\n\n**Front door** Traefik for TLS and host routing; Spring Cloud Gateway behind it for JWT, temple resolution and rate limits.\n\n**Authorization** Keycloak carries identity, temple memberships and a coarse role per temple; services enforce fine-grained permissions, cached per request.\n\n**Comms** REST for synchronous answers + **RabbitMQ, in-cluster**, published via transactional outbox. **`/api/v1/`, additive-only.**\n\n**Web** One Vite + React + TypeScript SPA (public + admin) · Ant Design · TanStack Query + Zustand · nginx container + CloudFront · **per-temple domains, admin and public on the same domain, as today**.\n\n**Android** One Expo app for staff, fundraisers and donors, role-driven from the backend · expo-router · read-only offline cache · FCM direct · **replaces `fundraiser-app`**.\n\n**Observability** Application logs → CloudWatch (JSON, 14-day retention); metrics → in-cluster Prometheus + Grafana; tracing deferred.\n\n**Repos** One per service (~18 total) + `platform-commons` + clients + manifests + infra.\n\n**Cross-temple screens: NONE.** Every screen is one temple. No data warehouse. Verified: today's PHP app has zero `DB::connection()` calls and one set of DB credentials — it already cannot read another temple.\n\n**Audit & activity logs** stay inside the temple's own schema. Audit is a library, not a service.\n\n**Migration** pgloader → staging → per-service split jobs; big-bang per temple; UAT → GNW/NEX → WHF → **Noida last**.\n\n**AI** **ISKCON-GPT** is the single AI platform — Python/FastAPI, **running on on-prem GPU hardware, outside AWS**. It both serves the platform and reads platform data via `/api/v1`. Hardware sizing is advisory; nothing is bought and eight assumptions are unconfirmed. The on-prem↔cloud link is still open.\n\n**Team: solo (+ Claude), no fixed deadline.**","x":2200,"y":-1560,"width":440,"height":1250,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"idp","type":"text","text":"## Identity Provider\nKeycloak (OIDC)\n**1 person = 1 account** across every product\nGoogle social login per temple","x":160,"y":-650,"width":340,"height":170,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"dns","type":"text","text":"**Route 53**\nper-temple domains","x":160,"y":-890,"width":260,"height":100},
		{"id":"traefik","type":"text","text":"**Traefik Ingress**\nbundled with k3s\nTLS termination · host routing","x":460,"y":-890,"width":300,"height":100,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"certmgr","type":"text","text":"**cert-manager**\nLet's Encrypt, issued automatically —\n**100 temple domains stay declarative**","x":800,"y":-890,"width":300,"height":100,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"gw","type":"text","text":"# API Gateway\nSpring Cloud Gateway\nverifies JWT locally · resolves temple · per-temple rate limits · routes\n**payment webhooks land here**","x":1140,"y":-890,"width":460,"height":100,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"ver","type":"text","text":"**API versioning**\n`/api/v1/…` in the path\n**additive-only** within a version\nold version kept until app telemetry shows it unused","x":1640,"y":-890,"width":400,"height":100,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"consumers","type":"text","text":"### Other consumers of the same `/api/v1` surface\n**Kiosk app** (Expo, in-temple) · **iskconnoida.org** public website (reads the Catalog API today) · **ISKCON-GPT** (Python/FastAPI, on-prem) · future partner integrations\n🔴 **`fundraiser-app` is retired** — its function moves into the single Android app above.","x":160,"y":-1160,"width":1880,"height":130,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"web","type":"text","text":"### React Web App — ONE SPA, public + admin\n\n**Vite + React + TypeScript** · **Ant Design**\n**TanStack Query** (server data) + **Zustand** (UI state)\nReact Router v7 · React Hook Form + Zod\nAPI client **generated from the OpenAPI spec**\nOIDC **Authorization Code + PKCE** → Keycloak\n`@ant-design/charts` · per-temple theming from the Tenant Registry\n\n**Per-temple domain, public pages and admin on the same domain — as today**\n\n_Client-rendered throughout. Verified: the current app emits no Open Graph tags and has no sitemap, so nothing is lost by dropping server rendering._","x":160,"y":-1490,"width":760,"height":310,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"mobile","type":"text","text":"### Android App — ONE app for everyone\nStaff · fundraisers · donors — **role decides what each sees, enforced by the backend**\n\n**Expo, built locally** (free, unqueued) · **expo-router**\n**Read-only offline cache** — writes blocked without a connection\nOIDC + PKCE via `expo-auth-session`, tokens in **SecureStore**\n**FCM direct** for push (Google's official Java SDK server-side)\nPayments: hand off to the gateway in a browser / web view","x":960,"y":-1490,"width":700,"height":310,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"cf","type":"text","text":"### CloudFront\n\nCDN in front of the\nweb app.\n\nAbsorbs ad-campaign\nspikes on donation\npages.\n\nPer-temple domains\nvia ACM.\n\n~$1–5/mo","x":1700,"y":-1490,"width":340,"height":310,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"sh-pool","type":"text","text":"### shard-pool-1 — **POOL**\nGNW · NEX · WHF","x":480,"y":690,"width":300,"height":150,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"d6","type":"text","text":"`events_db`","x":880,"y":690,"width":220,"height":90,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"d7","type":"text","text":"`ops_db`","x":1110,"y":690,"width":220,"height":90,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"d8","type":"text","text":"`notifications_db`","x":1340,"y":690,"width":220,"height":90,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"d9","type":"text","text":"`files_db`","x":1570,"y":690,"width":220,"height":90,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"d10","type":"text","text":"`timemgmt_db`","x":1800,"y":690,"width":220,"height":90,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"schemas","type":"text","text":"### Inside EVERY database: one schema per temple — `t_noida` · `t_gnw` · `t_nex` · `t_whf` · …\nNamed identically in silo and pool, so promoting a temple to its own shard is a **registry row change plus a schema move**.\nPostgreSQL cannot join or FK across databases **or** across hosts — service data ownership and temple separation are enforced by structure, not discipline.\n\n⚠️ ~240 tables per temple per service database drives the **~50-temple ceiling per shard**.","x":880,"y":810,"width":1140,"height":140,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"sh-future","type":"text","text":"### shard-pool-2 … n\non demand · ~25 planned, ~50 hard cap\n**Silo vs pool = a registry row, not a build-time property**","x":480,"y":870,"width":300,"height":100,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"ext-pay","type":"text","text":"### Payments\n**ICICI** — gateway · UPI mandates · CIB statement API\n**Razorpay**\nWebhooks → API Gateway → Donations+Payments","x":160,"y":1105,"width":290,"height":110,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"ext-msg","type":"text","text":"### Messaging\n**TimesMobile** — WhatsApp + SMS/OTP\n**AWS SES** — email\n**FCM** — Android push","x":480,"y":1105,"width":290,"height":110,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"ext-store","type":"text","text":"### Storage\n**AWS S3** — donor media, receipts, exports, database dumps\n_versioned bucket_","x":800,"y":1105,"width":290,"height":125,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"ext-ads","type":"text","text":"### Marketing\n**Meta Pixel + Conversions API** — donation events, including mandate debits","x":1120,"y":1105,"width":290,"height":135,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"ext-social","type":"text","text":"### Social login\n**Google** — per-temple OAuth clients, brokered through Keycloak","x":1440,"y":1105,"width":290,"height":125,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"ext-dev","type":"text","text":"### Devices & other\n**eSSL / eTimeTrackLite** biometric attendance\n**DHL** shipping · **Shopify** webhook","x":1760,"y":1105,"width":290,"height":125,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"backup","type":"text","text":"## Backup & disaster recovery\n· RDS automated backups, **30-day retention + PITR**, on every shard\n· Weekly `pg_dump` per `t_<temple>` schema → **versioned** S3 bucket with a lifecycle rule\n· S3 versioning **on from bucket creation**\n· ⚠️ RDS encryption at rest must be enabled **at instance creation** — it cannot be added afterwards\n· The cluster needs no backup: manifests and secrets are in git, data is in RDS\n\n🔴 **Quarterly restore drill in UAT** — restore one temple's schema, and rebuild the k3s node from scratch.\n**An untested backup is not a backup.**","x":2200,"y":1050,"width":440,"height":360,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"env-dev","type":"text","text":"## Dev (dev box)\n\n**Docker Compose** for infrastructure:\nPostgres as **two shards** · PgBouncer\nRabbitMQ · Keycloak\n\nThe service you are editing runs\n**natively from the IDE** — hot reload,\ndebugger attached\n\n_k3d only when testing manifests_","x":160,"y":1350,"width":420,"height":320,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"env-uat","type":"text","text":"## UAT (one EC2)\n\n**k3s** single node · Spot capacity\n\nPostgres **containers** as two shards\n\nSame manifests as prod, smaller values\n\n**Every tenant promotion, every temple\ncutover and every restore drill is\nrehearsed here first**","x":620,"y":1350,"width":420,"height":320,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"env-prod","type":"text","text":"## Production\n\n**k3s — single node** on **t4g (Graviton/ARM)**\n\nNode loss = **downtime, not data loss**:\nnew instance → install k3s → **Flux syncs from git**\n_rehearsed and timed in UAT; runbook kept_\n\n**RDS PostgreSQL:**\n· `shard-noida` — silo\n· `shard-pool-1` — GNW · NEX · WHF","x":1080,"y":1350,"width":520,"height":320,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"secrets","type":"text","text":"## Secrets — SOPS + age\n\nEncrypted **in git**, beside the\nmanifests that use them.\n\nFlux decrypts natively —\nnothing extra to run, $0.\n\n🔴 The `age` private key lives in the\ncluster **and** in the password\nmanager. Lose it and the secrets\nare unrecoverable.","x":1640,"y":1350,"width":400,"height":320,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"obs","type":"text","text":"### Observability\n**Application logs → CloudWatch Logs** — JSON on stdout, 14-day retention, ~$5/mo. This **retires the Jenkinsfile's SSH-and-grep check** for SQLSTATE errors.\n**Metrics** — Spring Actuator → in-cluster **Prometheus** + **Grafana** (~450 MB).\n**Every log line and metric tagged `tenant_id`** — this is where all-temple questions get answered.\nTracing deferred until service count justifies it.\n\n_Verified today: only host metrics (`CWAgent`) and RDS logs reach CloudWatch; application logs sit on container disks._","x":2200,"y":1450,"width":440,"height":300},
		{"id":"flux","type":"text","text":"## Flux — GitOps\nRuns **inside** the cluster and pulls from `dms-manifests`. The cluster is continuously reconciled to git: hand-edits and accidental deletions are reverted automatically, and CI never needs cluster-admin. ~300 MB.\n**\"Structure instead of discipline\" applied to deployment — the same principle that chose Model D.**","x":160,"y":1690,"width":1880,"height":80,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"repos","type":"text","text":"## Repositories — ONE PER SERVICE\n`api-gateway` · `auth-service` · `tenant-registry` · `users-service` · `donations-service` · `catalog-service` · `receipts-service` · `fundraising-service` · `events-service` · `ops-service` · `notifications-service` · `files-service` · `reporting-service` · (`timemgmt-service`)\n\n`platform-commons` — audit library · tenant context · error contract\n`dms-web` · `dms-mobile` · `dms-manifests` (Flux) · `dms-infra` (Terraform)\n\n⚠️ **What this choice requires:**\n· a **Maven package registry** for `platform-commons` — ✅ verified live on Forgejo 16.0.3\n· a **shared Jenkins pipeline template**, so ~18 Jenkinsfiles cannot drift\n· release discipline: shared-library change = release → bump → update each consumer\n· cross-service refactors span several pull requests","x":160,"y":1890,"width":700,"height":260,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"ci","type":"text","text":"## CI/CD\n**Forgejo → Jenkins → ECR**\n\nMaven builds the JAR natively on x86;\n`buildx` copies it onto an **ARM JRE base**\n— no emulated compilation\n\nJenkins writes the image tag into\n`dms-manifests` and stops.\n**It never holds cluster credentials.**\n\nRegistry-driven Flyway fan-out,\ngrouped by shard","x":900,"y":1890,"width":420,"height":250,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"localdev","type":"text","text":"## Local development\nA laptop cannot run 10 JVMs.\n\nCompose brings up **infrastructure\nonly**; you run the 1–3 services\nyou are editing from the IDE.\n\nTestcontainers give each test run\na real Postgres.","x":1350,"y":1890,"width":340,"height":250,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"testing","type":"text","text":"## Testing\n· **Unit** — JUnit 5\n· **Integration** — Testcontainers\n· **Contract** — Spring Cloud Contract, every service pair\n· **Web** — Vitest + RTL\n· **E2E** — Playwright on the donation flow\n· **Migration** — the reconciliation report is a release gate","x":1720,"y":1890,"width":320,"height":250,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"open","type":"text","text":"# Still open — verification tasks, not design gaps\n1. Verify **arm64** availability for any library with native (JNI) code, as dependencies are added\n2. Revisit HA (**three** servers, not two) when an hour of downtime becomes unacceptable\n3. Final boundaries inside `ops_db` as the long tail migrates\n4. Whether `notifications_db` and `files_db` stay separate — each extra service database lowers temples-per-shard\n5. Time Management app — out of scope for now","x":2200,"y":2000,"width":440,"height":300,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"mig-how","type":"text","text":"## MySQL → PostgreSQL — it is a SPLIT, not a copy\nOne MySQL database of ~240 tables becomes **ten PostgreSQL service databases**, each with a `t_<temple>` schema, with type conversion along the way.\n\n1. **pgloader** lands a faithful, type-converted copy of one temple's MySQL database into a **staging schema**\n2. **Per-service jobs** populate each service database from staging\n3. Rehearsed in UAT and run repeatedly until it is boring\n4. **Big-bang cutover per temple**; MySQL kept **read-only** as the rollback","x":160,"y":2310,"width":620,"height":200,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"mig-recon","type":"text","text":"## 🔴 Reconciliation — the release gate\nNo temple goes live until this passes:\n\n· **row counts** match per table\n· **sum of donation amounts matches to the paisa**\n· receipt-number sequences continuous, no gaps\n· spot-check of donor PII fields\n\n_Given the August 2026 data gap and the `1366 fundraiser_id` silent write losses, a migration that \"looks fine\" is not evidence._","x":820,"y":2310,"width":620,"height":200,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"onboard","type":"text","text":"## Tenant onboarding — automated\n1. Registry row created\n2. Shard chosen (join a pool, or open a silo)\n3. `CREATE SCHEMA t_<temple>` in all service databases\n4. Flyway fan-out for that schema\n5. Seed catalog + settings\n6. Keycloak: temple group + first admin\n7. DNS record + cert-manager certificate\n8. Smoke test → mark active\n\n_At 100 tenants this cannot be manual._","x":1480,"y":2310,"width":560,"height":200,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"ph0","type":"text","text":"### Phase 0 — Foundation\n· k3s + Traefik + cert-manager + Flux\n· API Gateway\n· Keycloak + Auth service\n· **Tenant Registry**\n· `platform-commons` + Maven registry\n· Jenkins pipeline template\n· CloudWatch logs + Prometheus/Grafana\n· Migration runner (registry-driven)\n\n**Plus: one rehearsed tenant promotion in UAT — scripted, timed, runbooked**","x":160,"y":2670,"width":440,"height":260,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"ph1","type":"text","text":"### Phase 1 — The money path\n· Users & People\n· Donations + Payments\n· Catalog & Settings\n· Receipts & 80G\n· Notifications · Files\n· Web app + Android app\n\n**Cutover: UAT → then GNW or NEX**\n(smallest risk first; MySQL kept read-only)","x":640,"y":2670,"width":440,"height":260,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"ph2","type":"text","text":"### Phase 2 — Around the money\n· Fundraising & links\n· POS & Cash\n· Events & Volunteering\n· Reporting & Exports\n\n**Cutover: WHF**","x":1120,"y":2670,"width":440,"height":260,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"ph3","type":"text","text":"### Phase 3 — Long tail, then Noida\n· HR & Attendance\n· Gifts & Inventory · TR books\n· Kiosk · shipping · tickets · wishes\n\n**Cutover: NOIDA LAST** — live traffic,\n~92k donations, ICICI mandates\n\n---\n_Time Management: out of scope until the platform is settled_","x":1600,"y":2670,"width":440,"height":260,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"legend","type":"text","text":"# DMS Platform — FINAL architecture\nJava/Spring Boot microservices · Model D data layer · self-hosted **k3s on Graviton** with **Flux** GitOps · **one Vite/React SPA** · **one Expo Android app** · **ISKCON-GPT** (Python/FastAPI) on on-prem GPU hardware.\n\nHistory in this folder: `target-architecture-as-stated.canvas` (v1, only what was stated) · `target-architecture-v2-100-tenants.canvas` (v2, database-per-temple — superseded) · `target-architecture-v3-model-d.canvas` (v3).\n_A separate multi-tenancy model-comparison canvas existed on 2026-09-24 and is no longer in the vault; its conclusions are preserved in the \"Deliberately NOT\" panel._\n\n**Nothing has been built. No change has been made on local or AWS. This is the agreed target for team discussion.**\n_2026-09-26_","x":100,"y":3020,"width":1100,"height":260},
		{"id":"gpu","type":"text","text":"### On-prem GPU hardware\n_advisory only — nothing purchased_\nUnit = NVIDIA RTX PRO 6000 Blackwell 96 GB (₹14–17 L/card, Sep 2026)\n· 25k/day → 1-card workstation, ~₹20–24 L\n· 50k/day → 2 cards, ~₹40–48 L\n· 1 lakh/day → 4 cards, ~₹80–95 L\n· 10 lakh/day → HGX H200 node, ~₹4.8–5.5 Cr\nServe by day, LoRA training at night on the lower tiers.","x":2740,"y":1470,"width":460,"height":170,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"link","type":"text","text":"### 🔴 Crossing the boundary — open\nHow on-prem reaches the cluster is **not yet decided**: site-to-site VPN, or a public API with mutual TLS.\n**Donor and sadhana data leaving AWS for an on-prem box is a data-governance question, not only a networking one.**","x":2740,"y":1670,"width":460,"height":80,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"gpt","type":"text","text":"# ISKCON-GPT\n**The AI platform** — Python · FastAPI\n\nONE service, not two. It carries:\n· the corpus-trained LLM + **RAG** over the Prabhupada corpus\n· **behaviour analysis** — devotee patterns over time\n· **sadhana prediction** and **counselling** responses\n\nThe platform calls it through the API gateway; it reads platform data back through **`/api/v1` with a service token**, like any other client.\n\n⚠️ Sized 2026-09-23 across four tiers (25k → 10 lakh queries/day). **Nothing bought. Eight assumptions still unconfirmed** — languages, model class, voice, festival-peak policy, training scope, outage tolerance, site power, and who runs it 24×7.","x":2740,"y":1110,"width":460,"height":330,"color":"6"}
	],
